Sonos-Web version 0.01
======================

The README is used to introduce the module and provide instructions on
how to install the module, any machine dependencies it may have (for
example C compilers and installed libraries) and any other information
that should be provided before the module is installed.

A README file is required for CPAN modules since CPAN extracts the
README file from a module distribution so that people browsing the
archive can use it get an idea of the modules uses. It is usually a
good idea to provide version information here so that people can
decide whether fixes for the module are worth downloading.

INSTALLATION

To install this module type the following:

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

SIMULATOR INTEGRATION TESTS

The test suite includes an integration test against FrankenSonos' fsonos-sim.
Both Nix shells provide the packaged `fsonos` executable and its `fsonos-sim`
alias, and set FSONOS_SIM_BIN for the integration test. The package pins the
upstream source and nightly toolchain. Outside Nix, build its `fsonos`
executable with `cd /path/to/frankensonos && cargo build --release --features
sim`, then put it on PATH or set FSONOS_SIM_BIN to its path. The simulator test
is skipped when the executable is unavailable; it starts and stops its own
local virtual system and does not require Sonos hardware.

PLAYER DISCOVERY CACHE

On the first run, players are found through UPnP discovery. Their device
description URLs are saved by player UUID in location_cache.json in the
working directory, alongside the music library and album art caches.
Later runs preload these URLs and continue normal network discovery.
Rediscovery updates changed URLs. Failed startup preloads are removed from
the cache; temporary device removals during normal operation remain cached.
Delete location_cache.json to start discovery without saved locations.

